  "notes": "Degree-nine specialization of a rational cuspidal pencil on X1(2,26). In the submitted model y^2=x^3+c*x^2+b*(1-b-c)*x, P=(0,0) and Q=(b,b) generate C2 x C26. The field is irreducible modulo3. Modulo7 it has three quadratic factors and one cubic factor; the elliptic point counts are 52,52,52,364. Thus the full torsion is exactly C2 x C26. One representative is submitted, in accordance with the census diamond-orbit convention.",
